Toggle a status bar that the window builds after the show

The style installs its event filter on a main window only when the
window holds a status bar at the polish. A program that builds the
status bar after the first show therefore leaves the window without the
filter. The keyboard shortcut then does nothing, and the bar ignores the
hidden state of the last session.

The style now installs the filter on every main window that the hiding
option covers. The shortcut finds the status bars of the window at the
time of the key. The work for one bar moves to the polish of the bar. A
bar of any age therefore installs its own filter, takes the saved hidden
state and announces the bar to the window manager. A window with a
status bar at the polish keeps the behaviour of before.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 9 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

